{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096411 :question/id #uuid "48334c0c-a49e-5dfb-9f8a-8caa0c22d1f9" :question/math-academy-id "e-3625" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=4e^x+ 3x^4 - x^2,$ find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each term using the constant multiple, exponential, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)\n&= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(4e^x+3x^4-x^2\\right) \\\\\n&= 4\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(e^x)\n + 3\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x^4)\n - \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x^2) \\\\\n&= 4e^x+3(4x^3)-2x \\\\\n&= 4e^x+12x^3-2x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}
